# Push & Publish HTML File

When the user asks to "push and publish" an HTML file, run the following shell command from the `test-pages` directory:

```bash
./push-publish.sh <filename>
```

- Replace `<filename>` with the HTML file the user is referring to (e.g. `global-tag-prod-publish.html`)
- The script commits, pushes to `main`, and prints the live GitHub Pages URL
- If `GITHUB_TOKEN` is set in the environment, it will be used; otherwise the baked-in token is the fallback
- After the push succeeds, share the live URL: `https://vijay-zeta.github.io/test-pages/<filename>`
